Feature: Transfer active files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder based on configuration in ingest_config_master

  As a data engineer,
  I want a Databricks PySpark script to transfer only active files from the vendor's S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder,
  ensuring files are not already present in either the Purgo or Archive S3 folders,
  and using S3 paths and active_flag from the ingest_config_master table.

  Background:
    Given the Databricks Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the configuration table is "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And AWS credentials "access_key" and "secret_key" are stored in Databricks secret scope "aws_keys"
    And the script retrieves S3 paths from columns "s3_vendor_path", "s3_landing_path", and "s3_archive_path" in ingest_config_master
    And only rows with "active_flag" = "A" (case-sensitive) in ingest_config_master are considered active
    And file name matching is performed on the file name only (not full path), case-sensitive, including file extension
    And only files in the root of the vendor S3 folder are considered (no recursion into subfolders)
    And the script does not overwrite files in the Purgo S3 folder; such files are skipped
    And the script does not delete files from the vendor S3 bucket after transfer (copy, not move)
    And the script does not update any status tables or logs unless specified in the scenario

  Scenario: Transfer a single active file that does not exist in Purgo or Archive S3 folders
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C001"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/" contains the file "file1.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/" does not contain "file1.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/" does not contain "file1.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file1.csv" is copied from "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/" to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/"
    And "file1.csv" remains in "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/"
    And "file1.csv" does not exist in "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/"
    And no files are overwritten in "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/"

  Scenario: Do not transfer file if it already exists in Purgo S3 folder
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C002"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveB/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/" contains the file "file2.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/" contains "file2.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file2.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/"
    And "file2.csv" remains in "s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/"
    And no files are overwritten in "s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/"

  Scenario: Do not transfer file if it already exists in Archive S3 folder
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C003"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveC/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/" contains the file "file3.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveC/" contains "file3.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file3.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/"
    And "file3.csv" remains in "s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/"
    And no files are overwritten in "s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/"

  Scenario: Do not transfer inactive files (active_flag != "A")
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C004"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderD/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingD/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveD/"  | "N"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderD/" contains the file "file4.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file4.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingD/"
    And "file4.csv" remains in "s3://vendor-bucket/folderD/"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if ingest_config_master row is missing required S3 path columns
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path | s3_landing_path | s3_archive_path | active_flag |
      | "C005"    | null           | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingE/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveE/" | "A" |
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing required S3 path(s) in ingest_config_master for config_id C005"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if AWS credentials are missing or invalid
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing AWS credentials in Databricks secret scope 'aws_keys'"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario Outline: Transfer multiple files, skipping those already present in Purgo or Archive
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C006"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderF/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingF/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveF/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderF/" contains the files
      | file_name      |
      | <file_name_1>  |
      | <file_name_2>  |
      | <file_name_3>  |
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingF/" contains the files
      | file_name      |
      | <purgo_file_1> |
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveF/" contains the files
      | file_name      |
      | <archive_file_1> |
    When the script is executed
    Then only the following files are copied from "s3://vendor-bucket/folderF/" to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingF/"
      | file_name      |
      | <expected_file_1> |
    And no files are overwritten in "s3://purgo-bucket/landingF/"

    Examples:
      | file_name_1 | file_name_2 | file_name_3 | purgo_file_1 | archive_file_1 | expected_file_1 |
      | "a.csv"     | "b.csv"     | "c.csv"     | "b.csv"      | "c.csv"        | "a.csv"         |
      | "x.txt"     | "y.txt"     | "z.txt"     | "z.txt"      | "y.txt"        | "x.txt"         |

  Scenario: Do not transfer files in subfolders when file_recursive_flag is not set
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag | file_recursive_flag |
      | "C007"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderG/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingG/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveG/"  | "A"         | null                |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderG/" contains the files
      | file_name           |
      | "rootfile.csv"      |
      | "subfolder/file5.csv" |
    When the script is executed
    Then only "rootfile.csv" is copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingG/"
    And "subfolder/file5.csv" is not copied

  Scenario: Raise error if S3 path is not a valid S3 URI
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         | active_flag |
      | "C008"    | "not-a-s3-path"        | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingH/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveH/" | "A" |
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid S3 URI in ingest_config_master for config_id C008"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if no active configuration exists
    Given ingest_config_master contains no rows with active_flag = "A"
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if vendor S3 folder is empty
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C009"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderI/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingI/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveI/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderI/" is empty
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file name is null or empty
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C010"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderJ/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingJ/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveJ/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderJ/" contains a file with no name or an empty string as name
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid file name encountered in vendor S3 folder for config_id C010"
    And no files are transferred for that file

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file name contains invalid characters
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C011"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderK/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingK/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveK/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderK/" contains the file "file:invalid.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid file name 'file:invalid.csv' in vendor S3 folder for config_id C011"
    And "file:invalid.csv" is not transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file extension is not allowed (e.g., only .csv and .txt allowed)
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C012"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingL/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveL/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/" contains the file "file6.exe"
    When the script is executed
    Then "file6.exe" is not transferred
    And a warning is logged with message "File extension '.exe' not allowed for file6.exe in config_id C012"

  Scenario: Transfer files for multiple active configurations
    Given ingest_config_master contains the following rows
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C013"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderM/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingM/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveM/"  | "A"         |
      | "C014"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderN/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingN/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveN/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderM/" contains the file "file7.csv"
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderN/" contains the file "file8.csv"
    And neither file exists in their respective Purgo or Archive S3 folders
    When the script is executed
    Then "file7.csv" is copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingM/"
    And "file8.csv" is copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingN/"

  Scenario: Raise error if Databricks secret scope is not accessible
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" is not accessible due to permissions
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Unable to access Databricks secret scope 'aws_keys' for AWS credentials"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario: Raise error if S3 access fails due to invalid credentials
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" contains invalid "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Failed to authenticate to S3 with provided credentials"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario: Raise error if S3 bucket or folder does not exist
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C015"    | "s3://nonexistent-bucket/folderO/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingO/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveO/"  | "A"         |
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "S3 bucket or folder 's3://nonexistent-bucket/folderO/' does not exist for config_id C015"
    And no files are transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file name matches in a case-insensitive manner (case-sensitive match required)
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C016"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderP/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingP/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveP/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderP/" contains the file "File9.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingP/" contains "file9.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then "File9.csv" is copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingP/"
    And "file9.csv" is not overwritten

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if ingest_config_master row is missing active_flag
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C017"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderQ/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingQ/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveQ/"  | null        |
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred for config_id "C017"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if ingest_config_master row has active_flag not equal to "A" (e.g., "Y", "1", "true")
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C018"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderR/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingR/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveR/"  | "Y"         |
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred for config_id "C018"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file name is duplicated in vendor S3 folder
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C019"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderS/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingS/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveS/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderS/" contains two files with the same name "file10.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Duplicate file name 'file10.csv' found in vendor S3 folder for config_id C019"
    And "file10.csv" is not transferred

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file size is zero bytes
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C020"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderT/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingT/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveT/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderT/" contains the file "file11.csv" with size 0 bytes
    When the script is executed
    Then "file11.csv" is not transferred
    And a warning is logged with message "File 'file11.csv' in vendor S3 folder for config_id C020 is empty and was skipped"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if file name contains whitespace at start or end
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | "C021"    | "s3://vendor-bucket/folderU/" | "s3://purgo-bucket/landingU/"  | "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveU/"  | "A"         |
    And the vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderU/" contains the file " file12.csv "
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "File name ' file12.csv ' contains leading or trailing whitespace in vendor S3 folder for config_id C021"
    And " file12.csv " is not transferred
